          "coreNotes": "\n            <div class=\"space-y-4 text-slate-200\">\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-rose-400\">⚠️ 1. Degradation Factors in Ethiopia</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed\">\n                  • <strong>Rapid Population Growth:</strong> Surging demand for farmland, fuelwood, and grazing land.<br>\n                  • <strong>Agricultural Encroachment:</strong> Clearing steep, fragile mountain slopes without soil conservation measures.<br>\n                  • <strong>Overgrazing:</strong> Excessive livestock numbers stripping natural grass cover, leaving bare topsoil exposed to rainfall impact.<br>\n                  • <strong>Soil Erosion:</strong> Water runoff washes away billions of tons of fertile highland topsoil annually into river basins (Abbay/Blue Nile, Tekeze, Awash).<br>\n                  • <strong>Climate Variability:</strong> Recurrent droughts followed by torrential rains accelerating gully erosion.\n                </p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-emerald-400\">🛡️ 2. Conservation Solutions</h4>\n                <ul class=\"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside\">\n                  <li><strong>Afforestation and Reforestation:</strong> Planting indigenous tree species (Acacia, Cordia africana, Hagenia abyssinica) on bare watersheds (Green Legacy Initiative).</li>\n                  <li><strong>Physical Soil and Water Conservation:</strong> Building stone bunds, hillside terraces, check dams across gullies, and contour plowing.</li>\n                  <li><strong>Area Enclosures:</strong> Fencing off degraded hillsides to allow natural vegetation regeneration without animal grazing.</li>\n                  <li><strong>Community Participation:</strong> Involving local farming communities in watershed planning, seedling nursery management, and forest protection.</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          ",
