          "coreNotes": "\n            <div class=\"space-y-4 text-slate-200\">\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-rose-400\">⚠️ 1. Defining Environmental Challenges</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed\">\n                  • <strong>Pollution:</strong> The introduction of harmful, toxic substances or energy (heat, noise, radiation) into the natural environment at levels that exceed the system's capacity to disperse, dilute, or render them harmless, causing detrimental changes to living organisms and ecosystems.<br>\n                  • <strong>Major Environmental Threats:</strong> Industrial chemical spills, untreated urban sewage in rivers (e.g. Akaki River), plastic waste clogging drainage, greenhouse gas emissions driving global warming, and extensive deforestation accelerating desertification.\n                </p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-emerald-400\">🛡️ 2. Protection and Restoration Strategies</h4>\n                <ul class=\"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside\">\n                  <li><strong>Pollution Prevention:</strong> Enforcing strict industrial effluent discharge standards and transitioning to zero-emission renewable energy (hydro, solar, wind).</li>\n                  <li><strong>Waste Management:</strong> Adopting the 3Rs (Reduce, Reuse, Recycle) and establishing sanitary engineered landfills.</li>\n                  <li><strong>Ecological Restoration:</strong> Mass afforestation, watershed rehabilitation, wetland protection, and soil conservation.</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          ",
