          "coreNotes": "\n            <div class=\"space-y-4 text-slate-200\">\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-amber-400\">📈 1. Understanding Demographic Overload</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed\">\n                  • <strong>Definition:</strong> <strong>Demographic overload</strong> occurs when the rate and volume of population growth substantially exceeds the carrying capacity of available resources, capital, infrastructure, and social services.<br>\n                  • <strong>Socio-Economic Symptoms:</strong><br>\n                  - Overcrowded classrooms with high student-to-teacher ratios.<br>\n                  - Acute shortages of hospital beds, medical personnel, and essential medicines.<br>\n                  - Proliferation of informal urban slum settlements lacking clean water and sanitation.<br>\n                  - High youth unemployment and informal underemployment.<br>\n                  - Severe environmental strain (accelerated deforestation, soil depletion, water shortages).\n                </p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-cyan-400\">💡 2. Strategic Policy Responses</h4>\n                <ul class=\"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside\">\n                  <li><strong>Universal Education:</strong> Especially female secondary and tertiary education, which correlates strongly with lower fertility rates and healthier families.</li>\n                  <li><strong>Voluntary Family Planning:</strong> Expanding accessible reproductive healthcare and awareness.</li>\n                  <li><strong>Job Creation & Industrialization:</strong> Fostering manufacturing and agro-processing industries to absorb growing workforces.</li>\n                  <li><strong>Decentralized Infrastructure:</strong> Developing secondary growth poles and regional towns to relieve pressure on capital cities.</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          ",
